# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizer build (README.md, Development). Only what lives for the whole process
# and is not Notolith's to free: the font stack, Qt's thread pool, and the one-time setup of third-party libraries.
# Not by library name (leak:libQt6Core would hide a QObject Notolith forgot to delete): by what leaks.
leak:QFontDatabase
leak:QFontEngine
leak:QFontPrivate
leak:QFontCache
leak:QFontconfigDatabase
leak:QFreetypeFace
leak:QTextEngine
leak:QTextLayout
leak:QPlatformFontDatabase
leak:QThreadPoolPrivate::startThread
leak:QCoreApplicationPrivate::init
leak:QApplicationPrivate::init
leak:QGuiApplicationPrivate
leak:hb_
leak:FT_
leak:FcInit
leak:FcConfig
leak:libfontconfig
leak:libharfbuzz
leak:libfreetype
# MicroTeX sets up its symbol tables once and never tears them down.
leak:tex::
leak:ensureInitialised
# PdfPage keeps its QLibrary for the process (libs/render/PdfPage.cpp).
leak:PdfPage.cpp
# A std::function a test keeps in a global to answer the next message box.
leak:onNextBox
# The graphics driver, loaded by Qt's platform plugin even offscreen.
leak:libnvidia
leak:libGLX
leak:libGLdispatch
leak:libEGL
leak:libX11
leak:libxcb
leak:libdbus
leak:libglib
leak:libgobject
leak:microtex
leak:libcrypto
leak:<unknown module>
